{{Quote|The Empire is building an armory in the center of town. They say it's a new complex office, but everyone knows the truth.|[[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]]|<ref name="Festive">{{Andor|What a Festive Evening}}</ref>}}
The '''Palmo armory''' was an [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[armory]] built in the [[city]] of [[Palmo]] on the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]].<ref name="Ever Been" /> The towering building began construction by the Galactic Empire the day after a clandestine Imperial meeting at the [[Maltheen Divide]], where top Imperial [[officer]]s discussed the [[Ghorman project]], involving the Empire's manipulation of Ghorman in order to control the [[Kalkite|valuable natural resources]] on the planet. Although the Empire did not have a large presence on Ghorman before the armory,<ref name="OYL" /> by [[3 BBY]], the armory was in-progress and stood tall over [[Palmo Plaza]], casting a shadow over the [[Monument to the Fallen]], a commemoration of the hundreds of [[Ghorman (people)|Ghorman people]] who had [[Death|died]] in a [[Tarkin Massacre|massacre]] at the hands of the Empire's [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Ever Been" /> By [[2 BBY]], the armory had been completed.<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref>

The armory's existence violated the [[Imperial Charter]]. Publicly, the Empire did not reveal the nature of the construction, and the Ghorman people were told the building was an annex. However, members of the [[Ghorman Front]] rebel movement did not believe the lies and suspected Imperial military involvement.<ref name="Ever Been" />

